Package: mmBPFA
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Modal Beta-Process Factor Analysis
Version: 1.1.0
Date: 2020-07-07
Author: Evan Jones [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Evan Jones <evan.a.jones3@gmail.com>
Description: A semi-parametric Bayesian factor analysis for multimodal data.
             Observed items with any mix of binary, ordinal, count and continuous
             margins are treated as monotone transformations of a latent Gaussian
             copula through the extended rank likelihood (Hoff 2007; Murray et al. 2013),
             so no margin has to be modelled. The number of dimensions is learned with a
             cumulative shrinkage prior over factors (Legramanti, Durante and Dunson 2020)
             and each item's inclusion on each factor is learned within factors (Schiavon,
             Canale and Dunson 2022), so the fit reports both how many dimensions the data
             support and which items load on each. Only observed cells enter the sampler,
             which runs in C++ with OpenMP, so its cost scales with the number of observed
             cells. Applications include dimension reduction, multidimensional scaling
             (item-response theory), and recommendation over sparse multimodal ratings.
